IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2016(i) TO (k): State option for certain individuals, interoperability and portability, and online transactions (7 U.S.C. 2016(i) to (k)): lines 1106-1198 of usc07-ch51.txt.
-- Subsections (a) to (g) are in snap3-s2016-a-to-g.l4 and subsection (h) in snap3-s2016-h.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE) with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say. Money is a NUMBER of dollars.
-- A duty without a stated time is answered "has done": JUST TRUE if done, NOTHING if not.
-- Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

-- THE DATES subsection (j) counts from and to, taken from its words.
-- src:1148 | Not later than October 1, 2002
@ref s 2016(j)(2) the last day for ensuring interoperability and portability (src:1148)
`s 2016(j)(2) the last day for ensuring interoperability and portability` MEANS Date 1 10 2002

-- src:1170 | incurred after February 11, 2000
@ref s 2016(j)(6)(A)(i) the day after which the first period of costs begins (src:1170)
`s 2016(j)(6)(A)(i) the day after which the first period of costs begins` MEANS Date 11 2 2000

-- src:1171 | incurred after September 30, 2002
@ref s 2016(j)(6)(A)(ii) the day after which the second period of costs begins (src:1171)
`s 2016(j)(6)(A)(ii) the day after which the second period of costs begins` MEANS Date 30 9 2002

§ `s 2016(i) -- State option to issue benefits to certain individuals made ineligible by welfare reform`

-- src:1107 | (1) In general
-- src:1108 | Notwithstanding any other provision of law, a State agency may, with the approval of the Secretary, issue benefits under this chapter to an individual who is ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program solely as a result of section 2015(o)(2) of this title or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8.
@ref s 2016(i)(1) a State agency may, with the Secretary's approval, issue benefits to an individual made ineligible solely by section 2015(o)(2) or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8 (src:1107-1108)
GIVEN `the individual is ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program solely as a result of section 2015(o)(2) of this title or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has the approval of the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(i)(1) the State agency may issue benefits under this chapter to the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual is ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program solely as a result of section 2015(o)(2) of this title or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to an individual who is ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program solely as a result of section 2015(o)(2) of this title or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8"
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `the State agency has the approval of the Secretary` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a State agency may, with the approval of the Secretary, issue benefits under this chapter"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1109 | (2) State payments to Secretary
-- src:1110 | (A) In general
-- src:1111 | Not later than the date the State agency issues benefits to individuals under this subsection, the State agency shall pay the Secretary, in accordance with procedures established by the Secretary, an amount that is equal to—
-- src:1112 | (i) the value of the benefits; and
-- src:1113 | (ii) the costs of issuing and redeeming benefits, and other Federal costs, incurred in providing the benefits, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(i)(2)(A) the amount the State agency pays the Secretary is the value of the benefits plus the costs of issuing and redeeming them and other Federal costs (src:1109-1113)
GIVEN `the value of the benefits in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of issuing and redeeming benefits, and other Federal costs, incurred in providing the benefits, as determined by the Secretary, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2016(i)(2)(A) the amount the State agency must pay the Secretary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the costs of issuing and redeeming benefits, and other Federal costs, incurred in providing the benefits, as determined by the Secretary, in dollars`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as determined by the Secretary"
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST costs THEN JUST (`the value of the benefits in dollars` PLUS costs)

-- src:1110 | (A) In general
-- src:1111 | Not later than the date the State agency issues benefits to individuals under this subsection, the State agency shall pay the Secretary, in accordance with procedures established by the Secretary, an amount that is equal to—
@ref s 2016(i)(2)(A) the State agency pays not later than the date it issues benefits (src:1110-1111)
GIVEN `the date on which the State agency pays the Secretary` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the State agency issues benefits to individuals under this subsection` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(i)(2)(A) the State agency paid the Secretary in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date on which the State agency pays the Secretary` AT MOST Day `the date on which the State agency issues benefits to individuals under this subsection` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than the date the State agency issues benefits to individuals under this subsection, the State agency shall pay the Secretary"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1114 | (B) Crediting
-- src:1115 | Notwithstanding section 3302(b) of title 31, payments received under subparagraph (A) shall be credited to the supplemental nutrition assistance program appropriation account or the account from which the costs were drawn, as appropriate, for the fiscal year in which the payment is received.
@ref s 2016(i)(2)(B) payments are credited to the program appropriation account or the account from which the costs were drawn (src:1114-1115)
GIVEN `the payment is one received under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(i)(2)(B) the payment is credited to the supplemental nutrition assistance program appropriation account or the account from which the costs were drawn, as appropriate, for the fiscal year in which the payment is received` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment is one received under subparagraph (A)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payments received under subparagraph (A)"
            NOTHING

-- src:1116 | (3) Reporting
