        IF `the State agency has submitted a plan to the Secretary that describes the conditions and procedures under which the benefits will be issued, including eligibility standards, benefit levels, and the methodology the State agency will use to determine amounts due the Secretary under paragraph (2)` AND `the State agency has obtained the approval of the Secretary for the plan` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To be eligible to issue benefits under this subsection, a State agency shall"
            -- note (conditions of eligibility, which do not by themselves make the State agency eligible)
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible to issue benefits under this subsection, a State agency shall— (A) submit a plan to the Secretary"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1122 | (5) Violations
-- src:1123 | A sanction, disqualification, fine, or other penalty prescribed under Federal law (including sections 2021 and 2024 of this title) shall apply to a violation committed in connection with a benefit issued under this subsection.
@ref s 2016(i)(5) the sanctions, disqualifications, fines and penalties of Federal law, including sections 2021 and 2024, apply to a violation in connection with a benefit issued under this subsection (src:1122-1123)
GIVEN `the violation was committed in connection with a benefit issued under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
