§ `s 2016(j) -- interoperability and portability of electronic benefit transfer transactions`

§§ `s 2016(j)(1) definitions`

-- src:1131 | (A) Electronic benefit transfer card
-- src:1132 | The term “electronic benefit transfer card” means a card that provides benefits under this chapter through an electronic benefit transfer service (as defined in subsection (h)(11)(A)).
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(A) the meaning of "electronic benefit transfer card" (src:1131-1132)
GIVEN `the card provides benefits under this chapter through an electronic benefit transfer service (as defined in subsection (h)(11)(A))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(A) the card is an electronic benefit transfer card` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the card provides benefits under this chapter through an electronic benefit transfer service (as defined in subsection (h)(11)(A))` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a card that provides benefits under this chapter through an electronic benefit transfer service"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1133 | (B) Electronic benefit transfer contract
-- src:1134 | The term “electronic benefit transfer contract” means a contract that provides for the issuance, use, or redemption of program benefits in the form of electronic benefit transfer cards.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(B) the meaning of "electronic benefit transfer contract" (src:1133-1134)
GIVEN `the contract provides for the issuance, use, or redemption of program benefits in the form of electronic benefit transfer cards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(B) the contract is an electronic benefit transfer contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract provides for the issuance, use, or redemption of program benefits in the form of electronic benefit transfer cards` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a contract that provides for the issuance, use, or redemption of program benefits in the form of electronic benefit transfer cards"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1135 | (C) Interoperability
-- src:1136 | The term “interoperability” means a system that enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be redeemed in any State.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(C) the meaning of "interoperability" (src:1135-1136)
GIVEN `the system enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be redeemed in any State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(C) the system provides interoperability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the system enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be redeemed in any State` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a system that enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be redeemed in any State"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1137 | (D) Interstate transaction
-- src:1138 | The term “interstate transaction” means a transaction that is initiated in 1 State by the use of an electronic benefit transfer card that is issued in another State.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(D) the meaning of "interstate transaction" (src:1137-1138)
GIVEN `the transaction is initiated in 1 State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is initiated by the use of an electronic benefit transfer card` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the card is issued in another State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(D) the transaction is an interstate transaction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transaction is initiated in 1 State` AND `the transaction is initiated by the use of an electronic benefit transfer card` AND `the card is issued in another State` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a transaction that is initiated in 1 State by the use of an electronic benefit transfer card that is issued in another State"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1139 | (E) Portability
-- src:1140 | The term “portability” means a system that enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be used in any State by a household to purchase food at a retail food store or wholesale food concern approved under this chapter.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(E) the meaning of "portability" (src:1139-1140)
GIVEN `the system enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be used in any State by a household to purchase food at a retail food store or wholesale food concern approved under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(E) the system provides portability` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the system enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be used in any State by a household to purchase food at a retail food store or wholesale food concern approved under this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a system that enables program benefits in the form of an electronic benefit transfer card to be used in any State by a household to purchase food"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1141 | (F) Settling
-- src:1142 | The term “settling” means movement, and reporting such movement, of funds from an electronic benefit transfer card issuer that is located in 1 State to a retail food store, or wholesale food concern, that is located in another State, to accomplish an interstate transaction.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(F) the meaning of "settling" (src:1141-1142)
GIVEN `the movement of funds, and the reporting of it, is from an electronic benefit transfer card issuer located in 1 State to a retail food store, or wholesale food concern, located in another State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the movement is made to accomplish an interstate transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(F) the movement is settling` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the movement of funds, and the reporting of it, is from an electronic benefit transfer card issuer located in 1 State to a retail food store, or wholesale food concern, located in another State` AND `the movement is made to accomplish an interstate transaction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means movement, and reporting such movement, of funds from an electronic benefit transfer card issuer that is located in 1 State to a retail food store, or wholesale food concern, that is located in another State, to accomplish an interstate transaction"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1143 | (G) Smart card
-- src:1144 | The term “smart card” means an intelligent benefit card described in section 2026(f) of this title.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(G) the meaning of "smart card" (src:1143-1144)
-- The text points to section 2026(f), which is outside this text: the answer is an input.
GIVEN `s 2026(f) the card is an intelligent benefit card described in section 2026(f)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(G) the card is a smart card` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2026(f) the card is an intelligent benefit card described in section 2026(f)`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "means an intelligent benefit card described in section 2026(f) of this title"
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST b THEN JUST b

-- src:1145 | (H) Switching
-- src:1146 | The term “switching” means the routing of an intrastate or interstate transaction that consists of transmitting the details of a transaction electronically recorded through the use of an electronic benefit transfer card in one State to the issuer of the card that may be in the same or different State.
@ref s 2016(j)(1)(H) the meaning of "switching" (src:1145-1146)
GIVEN `the routing is of an intrastate or interstate transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the routing consists of transmitting the details of a transaction electronically recorded through the use of an electronic benefit transfer card in one State to the issuer of the card, in the same or a different State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(1)(H) the routing is switching` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the routing is of an intrastate or interstate transaction` AND `the routing consists of transmitting the details of a transaction electronically recorded through the use of an electronic benefit transfer card in one State to the issuer of the card, in the same or a different State` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the routing of an intrastate or interstate transaction that consists of transmitting the details of a transaction electronically recorded through the use of an electronic benefit transfer card in one State to the issuer of the card"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2016(j)(2) to (6) the requirement, its cost, exemptions and funding`

-- src:1147 | (2) Requirement
-- src:1148 | Not later than October 1, 2002, the Secretary shall ensure that systems that provide for the electronic issuance, use, and redemption of program benefits in the form of electronic benefit transfer cards are interoperable, and supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are portable, among all States.
@ref s 2016(j)(2) the Secretary ensures by 1 October 2002 that electronic benefit transfer systems are interoperable and benefits are portable among all States (src:1147-1148)
GIVEN `the date on which the Secretary ensured that the systems are interoperable and the benefits are portable among all States` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(2) the Secretary ensured interoperability and portability in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the Secretary ensured that the systems are interoperable and the benefits are portable among all States`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no date was supplied, and whether the Secretary has ensured it yet depends on today's date, which the text does not give
            NOTHING
        WHEN JUST ensured THEN
            IF Day ensured AT MOST Day `s 2016(j)(2) the last day for ensuring interoperability and portability`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than October 1, 2002, the Secretary shall ensure that systems that provide for the electronic issuance, use, and redemption of program benefits in the form of electronic benefit transfer cards are interoperable"
                JUST FALSE

-- src:1149 | (3) Cost
-- src:1150 | The cost of achieving the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2) shall not be imposed on any retail store, or any wholesale food concern, approved to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2016(j)(3) the cost of interoperability and portability is not imposed on any approved retail store or wholesale food concern (src:1149-1150)
GIVEN `the store or concern is approved to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(3) the cost of achieving the interoperability and portability may be imposed on the retail store or wholesale food concern` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the store or concern is approved to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be imposed on any retail store, or any wholesale food concern, approved to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any retail store, or any wholesale food concern, approved to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            NOTHING

-- src:1156 | (A) Contracts
-- src:1157 | The requirements of paragraph (2) shall not apply to the transfer of benefits under an electronic benefit transfer contract before the expiration of the term of the contract if the contract—
-- src:1158 | (i) is entered into before the date that is 30 days after the regulations are promulgated under paragraph (4); and
-- src:1159 | (ii) expires after October 1, 2002.
@ref s 2016(j)(5)(A) the requirements of paragraph (2) do not apply to an electronic benefit transfer contract entered into early and expiring after 1 October 2002 (src:1156-1159)
-- In plain words: until a contract ends, the interoperability and portability requirement does not apply to transfers under it, if the contract was entered into before the date 30 days after the regulations under paragraph (4) are promulgated and expires after 1 October 2002.
GIVEN `the date on which the contract is entered into` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the regulations are promulgated under paragraph (4)` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the contract expires` IS A DATE
      `the transfer of benefits is made before the expiration of the term of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(5)(A) the requirements of paragraph (2) apply to the transfer of benefits under the electronic benefit transfer contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transfer of benefits is made before the expiration of the term of the contract` AND Day `the date on which the contract is entered into` LESS THAN Day `the date on which the regulations are promulgated under paragraph (4)` PLUS 30 AND Day `the date on which the contract expires` GREATER THAN Day `s 2016(j)(2) the last day for ensuring interoperability and portability` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of paragraph (2) shall not apply to the transfer of benefits under an electronic benefit transfer contract before the expiration of the term of the contract if the contract"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the contract— (i) is entered into before the date that is 30 days after the regulations are promulgated under paragraph (4); and (ii) expires after October 1, 2002."
            -- note (the exemption is not met; paragraph (2) is not said to apply, only that this exemption does not)
            NOTHING

-- src:1160 | (B) Waiver
-- src:1161 | At the request of a State agency, the Secretary may provide 1 waiver to temporarily exempt, for a period ending on or before the date specified under clause (iii), the State agency from complying with the requirements of paragraph (2), if the State agency—
-- src:1162 | (i) establishes to the satisfaction of the Secretary that the State agency faces unusual technological barriers to achieving by October 1, 2002, the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2);
-- src:1163 | (ii) demonstrates that the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program would be served by granting the waiver with respect to the electronic benefit transfer system used by the State agency to administer the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1164 | (iii) specifies a date by which the State agency will achieve the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2).
@ref s 2016(j)(5)(B) the Secretary may provide one waiver to a State agency that shows unusual technological barriers, the best interest of the program, and a date (src:1160-1164)
GIVEN `the State agency requests the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of waivers the Secretary has already provided to the State agency` IS A NUMBER
      `the State agency establishes to the satisfaction of the Secretary that it faces unusual technological barriers to achieving by October 1, 2002, the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency demonstrates that the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program would be served by granting the waiver` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency specifies a date by which it will achieve the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(5)(B) the Secretary may provide the waiver` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency requests the waiver` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the request of a State agency"
            NOTHING
        IF `the number of waivers the Secretary has already provided to the State agency` AT LEAST 1 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary may provide 1 waiver"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST
                `the State agency establishes to the satisfaction of the Secretary that it faces unusual technological barriers to achieving by October 1, 2002, the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2)`
              , `the State agency demonstrates that the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program would be served by granting the waiver`
              , JUST `the State agency specifies a date by which it will achieve the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2)`
              )

-- src:1160 | (B) Waiver
-- src:1161 | At the request of a State agency, the Secretary may provide 1 waiver to temporarily exempt, for a period ending on or before the date specified under clause (iii), the State agency from complying with the requirements of paragraph (2), if the State agency—
-- src:1162 | (i) establishes to the satisfaction of the Secretary that the State agency faces unusual technological barriers to achieving by October 1, 2002, the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2);
-- src:1163 | (ii) demonstrates that the best interest of the supplemental nutrition assistance program would be served by granting the waiver with respect to the electronic benefit transfer system used by the State agency to administer the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:1164 | (iii) specifies a date by which the State agency will achieve the interoperability and portability required under paragraph (2).
@ref s 2016(j)(5)(B) the waiver period ends on or before the date the State agency specifies (src:1160-1164)
GIVEN `the date on which the waiver period ends` IS A DATE
      `the date the State agency specifies under clause (iii)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(5)(B) the waiver period is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date on which the waiver period ends` AT MOST Day `the date the State agency specifies under clause (iii)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period ending on or before the date specified under clause (iii)"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1165 | (C) Smart card systems
-- src:1166 | The Secretary shall allow a State agency that is using smart cards for the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to comply with the requirements of paragraph (2) at such time after October 1, 2002, as the Secretary determines that a practicable technological method is available for interoperability with electronic benefit transfer cards.
@ref s 2016(j)(5)(C) the Secretary allows a State agency using smart cards to comply at a time after 1 October 2002 when a practicable method exists (src:1165-1166)
GIVEN `the State agency is using smart cards for the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(5)(C) the Secretary must allow the State agency to comply with paragraph (2) at the later time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency is using smart cards for the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a State agency that is using smart cards for the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits"
            NOTHING

-- src:1167 | (6) Funding
-- src:1168 | (A) In general
-- src:1169 | In accordance with regulations promulgated by the Secretary, the Secretary shall pay 100 percent of the costs incurred by a State agency under this chapter for switching and settling interstate transactions—
-- src:1170 | (i) incurred after February 11, 2000, and before October 1, 2002, if the State agency uses the standard of interoperability and portability adopted by a majority of State agencies; and
-- src:1171 | (ii) incurred after September 30, 2002, if the State agency uses the uniform national standard of interoperability and portability adopted under paragraph (4)(A).
@ref s 2016(j)(6)(A) the Secretary pays 100 percent of a State agency's costs of switching and settling interstate transactions in the two periods (src:1167-1171)
-- In plain words: the Secretary pays all of a State agency's costs of switching and settling interstate transactions that were incurred after 11 February 2000 and before 1 October 2002 if the State agency used the standard a majority of State agencies adopted,
-- and all such costs incurred after 30 September 2002 if it used the uniform national standard adopted under paragraph (4)(A). A cost incurred on 11 February 2000 itself is not "after" that day; one incurred on 1 October 2002 is after 30 September 2002.
GIVEN `the date on which the cost was incurred` IS A DATE
      `the cost is for switching and settling interstate transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency uses the standard of interoperability and portability adopted by a majority of State agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency uses the uniform national standard of interoperability and portability adopted under paragraph (4)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(6)(A) the Secretary must pay 100 percent of the cost` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the cost is for switching and settling interstate transactions` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the costs incurred by a State agency under this chapter for switching and settling interstate transactions"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date on which the cost was incurred` GREATER THAN Day `s 2016(j)(6)(A)(i) the day after which the first period of costs begins` AND Day `the date on which the cost was incurred` LESS THAN Day `s 2016(j)(2) the last day for ensuring interoperability and portability` THEN
            IF `the State agency uses the standard of interoperability and portability adopted by a majority of State agencies` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the State agency uses the standard of interoperability and portability adopted by a majority of State agencies"
                -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
                JUST FALSE
        IF Day `the date on which the cost was incurred` GREATER THAN Day `s 2016(j)(6)(A)(ii) the day after which the second period of costs begins` THEN
            IF `the State agency uses the uniform national standard of interoperability and portability adopted under paragraph (4)(A)` THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE
                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the State agency uses the uniform national standard of interoperability and portability adopted under paragraph (4)(A)"
                -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
                JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) incurred after February 11, 2000, and before October 1, 2002, if the State agency uses the standard of interoperability and portability adopted by a majority of State agencies"
            NOTHING

-- src:1172 | (B) Limitation
-- src:1173 | The total amount paid to State agencies for each fiscal year under subparagraph (A) shall not exceed $500,000.
@ref s 2016(j)(6)(B) the total paid to State agencies in a fiscal year under subparagraph (A) does not exceed $500,000 (src:1172-1173)
GIVEN `the total amount paid to State agencies for the fiscal year under subparagraph (A) in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(j)(6)(B) the total amount paid is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the total amount paid to State agencies for the fiscal year under subparagraph (A) in dollars` AT MOST 500000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not exceed $500,000"
            JUST FALSE

§ `s 2016(k) -- acceptance of program benefits through online transactions`

-- src:1175 | (1) In general
-- src:1176 | Subject to paragraph (4), the Secretary shall approve retail food stores to accept benefits from recipients of supplemental nutrition assistance through on-line transactions.
@ref s 2016(k)(1) the Secretary approves retail food stores to accept benefits through on-line transactions, subject to paragraph (4) (src:1175-1176)
GIVEN `the retail food store meets the requirements of paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (4) permits approval of the store` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(k)(1) the Secretary must approve the retail food store to accept benefits through on-line transactions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the retail food store meets the requirements of paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A retail food store seeking to accept benefits from recipients of supplemental nutrition assistance through on-line transactions shall"
            -- note (a failed condition; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `paragraph (4) permits approval of the store` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to paragraph (4)"
            NOTHING
        IF `the retail food store meets the requirements of paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the store meets the requirements of paragraph (2), including the Secretary's other criteria, was not supplied
            NOTHING

-- src:1177 | (2) Requirements to accept benefits
-- src:1178 | A retail food store seeking to accept benefits from recipients of supplemental nutrition assistance through on-line transactions shall—
-- src:1179 | (A) establish recipient protections regarding privacy, ease of use, access, and support similar to the protections provided for transactions made in retail food stores;
-- src:1180 | (B) ensure benefits are not used to pay delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges;
-- src:1181 | (C) clearly notify participating households at the time a food order is placed—
-- src:1182 | (i) of any delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge associated with the food purchase; and
-- src:1183 | (ii) that any such fee cannot be paid with benefits provided under this chapter;
-- src:1184 | (D) ensure the security of on-line transactions by using the most effective technology available that the Secretary considers appropriate and cost-effective and that is comparable to the security of transactions at retail food stores; and
-- src:1185 | (E) meet other criteria as established by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(k)(2) a retail food store seeking to accept benefits on-line meets the requirements of subparagraphs (A) to (E) (src:1177-1185)
GIVEN `the store establishes recipient protections regarding privacy, ease of use, access, and support similar to the protections provided for transactions made in retail food stores` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store ensures benefits are not used to pay delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store clearly notifies participating households at the time a food order is placed of any delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge associated with the food purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store clearly notifies participating households at the time a food order is placed that any such fee cannot be paid with benefits provided under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store ensures the security of on-line transactions by using the most effective technology available that the Secretary considers appropriate and cost-effective and that is comparable to the security of transactions at retail food stores` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the store meets other criteria as established by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(k)(2) the retail food store meets the requirements of paragraph (2)` MEANS
    `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST
        JUST `the store establishes recipient protections regarding privacy, ease of use, access, and support similar to the protections provided for transactions made in retail food stores`
      , JUST `the store ensures benefits are not used to pay delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges`
      , JUST `the store clearly notifies participating households at the time a food order is placed of any delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge associated with the food purchase`
      , JUST `the store clearly notifies participating households at the time a food order is placed that any such fee cannot be paid with benefits provided under this chapter`
      , `the store ensures the security of on-line transactions by using the most effective technology available that the Secretary considers appropriate and cost-effective and that is comparable to the security of transactions at retail food stores`
      , `the store meets other criteria as established by the Secretary`
      )

-- src:1180 | (B) ensure benefits are not used to pay delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges;
@ref s 2016(k)(2)(B) benefits are not used to pay delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges (src:1180)
-- In plain words: a household cannot use SNAP benefits to pay a delivery, ordering, convenience or other fee or charge on an on-line food order.
GIVEN `the charge is a delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(k)(2)(B) the benefits may be used to pay the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the charge is a delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ensure benefits are not used to pay delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fees or charges"
            NOTHING

-- src:1186 | (3) State agency action
-- src:1187 | Each State agency shall ensure that recipients of supplemental nutrition assistance can use benefits on-line as described in this subsection as appropriate.
@ref s 2016(k)(3) each State agency ensures that recipients can use benefits on-line as appropriate (src:1186-1187)
GIVEN `the State agency has ensured that recipients of supplemental nutrition assistance can use benefits on-line as described in this subsection as appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(k)(3) the State agency has done what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has ensured that recipients of supplemental nutrition assistance can use benefits on-line as described in this subsection as appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the State agency must ensure it
            NOTHING

-- src:1188 | (4) Demonstration project on acceptance of benefits through on-line transactions
-- src:1189 | (A) In general
-- src:1190 | Before the Secretary authorizes implementation of paragraph (1) in all States, the Secretary shall carry out a number of demonstration projects as determined by the Secretary to test the feasibility of allowing retail food stores to accept benefits through on-line transactions.
@ref s 2016(k)(4)(A) the Secretary carries out demonstration projects before authorizing on-line acceptance in all States (src:1188-1190)
GIVEN `the Secretary has authorized implementation of paragraph (1) in all States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has carried out a number of demonstration projects as determined by the Secretary to test the feasibility of allowing retail food stores to accept benefits through on-line transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(k)(4)(A) the Secretary carried out the demonstration projects before authorizing implementation in all States` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Secretary has authorized implementation of paragraph (1) in all States` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before the Secretary authorizes implementation of paragraph (1) in all States"
            NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary has carried out a number of demonstration projects as determined by the Secretary to test the feasibility of allowing retail food stores to accept benefits through on-line transactions` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before the Secretary authorizes implementation of paragraph (1) in all States, the Secretary shall carry out a number of demonstration projects"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:1191 | (B) Demonstration projects
-- src:1192 | To be eligible to participate in a demonstration project under subparagraph (A), a retail food store shall submit to the Secretary for approval a plan that includes—
-- src:1193 | (i) a method of ensuring that benefits may be used to purchase only eligible items under this chapter;
-- src:1194 | (ii) a description of the method of educating participant households about the availability and operation of on-line purchasing;
-- src:1195 | (iii) adequate testing of the on-line purchasing option prior to implementation;
-- src:1196 | (iv) the provision of data as requested by the Secretary for purposes of analyzing the impact of the project on participant access, ease of use, and program integrity;
-- src:1197 | (v) reports on progress, challenges, and results, as determined by the Secretary; and
-- src:1198 | (vi) such other criteria, including security criteria, as established by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(k)(4)(B) a retail food store's plan for a demonstration project includes the six items listed (src:1191-1198)
GIVEN `the plan includes a method of ensuring that benefits may be used to purchase only eligible items under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes a description of the method of educating participant households about the availability and operation of on-line purchasing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes adequate testing of the on-line purchasing option prior to implementation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes the provision of data as requested by the Secretary for purposes of analyzing the impact of the project on participant access, ease of use, and program integrity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes reports on progress, challenges, and results, as determined by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the plan includes such other criteria, including security criteria, as established by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(k)(4)(B) the plan includes what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST
        JUST `the plan includes a method of ensuring that benefits may be used to purchase only eligible items under this chapter`
      , JUST `the plan includes a description of the method of educating participant households about the availability and operation of on-line purchasing`
      , JUST `the plan includes adequate testing of the on-line purchasing option prior to implementation`
      , JUST `the plan includes the provision of data as requested by the Secretary for purposes of analyzing the impact of the project on participant access, ease of use, and program integrity`
      , `the plan includes reports on progress, challenges, and results, as determined by the Secretary`
      , `the plan includes such other criteria, including security criteria, as established by the Secretary`
      )
